Delvers Frieren adds Frieren as a unique recruit in Custom Expedition and in the guild, with her own biography and portraits, the legendary Elven Archmage background and the Booklover trait. Her story follows her search for rare spells into the awakened dungeon core. She is a character pack for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/12]Delvers Core[/url].

The guild charges technique books to recruit her: one book for each started 150 gold of the usual price, with a minimum of one. Once Frieren has joined a campaign, she will not be generated again, even if she later dies. Elven Archmage lets her use fire, water and nature magic with the appropriate staffs. Booklover can also appear on characters from the game's original races. Using a technique book grants two main skill points, two secondary skill points and a temporary mood boost.

Frieren also casts her own spell Zoltraak: from a turning magic circle she channels a beam for three seconds that strikes the first enemy in a line with 15 hits of 40% of her magic attack each, and each hit lowers physical and magic resistance for a while. Casting, the shot and the beam have their own sounds. An obstacle in the way catches the beam; destructible obstacles take the damage, including your own buildings, trees and ore. Frieren learns Zoltraak in existing campaigns too, and the save keeps it, so that save then needs Frieren 0.5.0 or later.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/12]Delvers Core[/url] 0.5.0 or later, Windows x64, Dungeon Settlers DS_B.0.4.29 (Steam build 25846389) and BepInEx 6 for Unity IL2CPP x64, tested with 6.0.0-be.788. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/5]Extended Hotbar[/url] is optional.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Back up your saves first. Install Delvers Core, then extract the Frieren ZIP into the game folder; it already contains the required folders. If an old DungeonSettlersFrierenPortrait.dll is still in BepInEx/plugins/, Mods/ or UserLibs/, remove it.

[size=4][b]Reporting problems[/b][/size]

Please include your game build, BepInEx version and the log.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]

Made by Fre-yin; Frieren's portraits are original pixel artwork. Source code: [url=https://github.com/Fre-yin/DNST-Delvers-Frieren]github.com/Fre-yin/DNST-Delvers-Frieren[/url]. MIT license for the mod code; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES for everything else. An unofficial community project, not made by CanOpener.
